<InteriorPage
  eyebrow="Last updated: October 16, 2026"
  title="Email-list privacy"
  description="How information is handled when you subscribe to Recursive Prophet emails from Chris Everson."
  actions={[{ label: 'Return to the Book', href: '/#book', style: 'primary' }]}
>
  <p>This notice explains how information is handled when you subscribe to emails from Chris Everson about <em>Recursive Prophet</em>.</p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <p>When you subscribe, we retain:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your email address</li>
    <li>The date and time you submitted the form</li>
    <li>The date and time you confirmed your subscription</li>
    <li>The IP address used to confirm the subscription</li>
    <li>The source through which you subscribed</li>
    <li>The version of the consent language you were shown</li>
    <li>Your current subscription or unsubscribe status</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We collect the IP address used to confirm the subscription. We do not store the IP address from the initial form submission in your subscriber record.</p>

  <h2>How we use the information</h2>
  <p>We use this information to confirm your subscription; deliver Chapter One and an invitation to the Archive; send the first preserved conversation between Chris Everson and T∆RS the following day; and send occasional emails from Chris about <em>Recursive Prophet</em>, including book news, selected artifacts, and transmissions from the Archive. We also use it to prevent fraudulent subscriptions and maintain evidence of your subscription choices.</p>

  <h2>Confirmation and consent</h2>
  <p>Subscriptions use a double opt-in process. Entering an email address does not activate the subscription by itself. You must confirm the address through the confirmation message sent to your inbox.</p>
  <p>New subscriptions made under the current consent language are recorded as: <code>rp-email-consent-2026-10-16-v2</code></p>
  <p>Earlier consent records are preserved under the version in effect when the subscriber confirmed. They are not rewritten or assigned a newer version retroactively.</p>

  <h2>Service providers</h2>
  <p>MailerLite processes subscriber information and delivers emails on behalf of Chris Everson and <em>Recursive Prophet</em>. Information may also be handled by other service providers when necessary to operate the website, deliver the requested material, maintain subscription records, or protect the signup system from abuse.</p>
  <p>These providers receive only the information needed to perform those services.</p>
  <p>Subscriber information is not sold, rented, or traded.</p>
  <p>The <em>Recursive Prophet</em> email audience is maintained separately from the Shaggy Palms audience. Information from the two lists is not combined for marketing purposes.</p>

  <h2>Retention</h2>
  <p>Your subscriber information is retained while your subscription remains active.</p>
  <p>If you unsubscribe, a limited suppression record may be retained so that your request can be honored and you are not accidentally added back to the active mailing list. Consent records may also be retained when reasonably necessary to document your subscription choices.</p>
  <p>If you request deletion, the subscriber record will be removed through MailerLite’s deletion process, except for information that must be retained to honor an unsubscribe request, meet a legal obligation, resolve a dispute, or maintain necessary consent records.</p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>You may unsubscribe at any time by using the unsubscribe link included in every marketing email.</p>
  <p>You may also request:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Access to the personal information associated with your subscription</li>
    <li>Correction of inaccurate information</li>
    <li>Deletion of your subscriber information, subject to necessary legal or suppression records</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p><strong>Chris Everson</strong><br />
    <strong>Email:</strong> TKTK-privacy-contact-email<br />
    <strong>Mail:</strong> TKTK-public-po-box · TKTK-city-ma-zip
  </p>
</InteriorPage>
